[{"id":"VRCE-6-112-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":1,"english":"Behold the beautiful Yamunā, Yamunā, having picturesque forest on its bank and the pleasant hermitage of Bharadvāja. Behold there the sacred river Ganges, dividing itself into three branches.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.449,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bd4725db8468910332dfb46e23d2b101b6208849c15fd4d889851233b2c72d87","compact":"7267faeba3604f76f175ac5b0e81f955f7f9c5276a5f9c3f6677dd5b59ed99a3","nasal":"c5d092fe41a12a5b66ec7fb4c525fd2e5ec68ffc6f468163d3f3b087acb8a519"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":2,"english":"Do you behold, O Sita, Kiskindha, having beautiful gardens, the pleasant city of Sugrīva, where Vālī was slain by me.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.404,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"16ba5d32b99b55abdc8a009fcd25152dc78df4d54120d3ac338dbcb1f270c189","compact":"63657e3b56a2831f1c9e5570ca476ea8a3c1890871d33ac35959ed1b4810f80c","nasal":"25ec58d3e6ff2476e0216716fa729a3914af99fae7f94d3c6a735cb2522e0b09"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":3,"english":"Being thus addressed by Rāma, all the leading monkeys bears as well as the Rākşasa Vibhīşaņa said with folded hands.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.132,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-122-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bfda725afd543e263e3aab96e4dc66466f245a7bb674b67e5f4d0b8b80b7eec6","compact":"e1574ed67187419f80ca888ac7789b4958cd06eca54038dbb2a00bd0fd691984","nasal":"e1574ed67187419f80ca888ac7789b4958cd06eca54038dbb2a00bd0fd691984"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":4,"english":"He saw at a distance of one crosa from Ayodhyā Bharata wearing the skin of an antelope, poorly, greatly reduced, living in a hermitage, wearing matted hairs, having his body covered with dirt, greatly pulled down in consequence of his brother's disaster, living on roots and fruits, self-controlled, living the life of an ascetic, observing pious observances, with a bundle of clotted hairs on his head, wearing bark and deer skin, having control over his passions and senses, effulgent like Brahmarşis, ruling the earth always placing the sandals before him, protecting people of four Varnas against all fear, with courtiers, priests leading a holy life and soldiers all wearing red clothes around him. *The country of Bharata's maternal uncle.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.172,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-125-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"924519056cf71665347e73d54b599bb8389af3b8044a60a9bd6fb64c6a6f6516","compact":"c8c81b7a7c1fe27add75958950dd009b0058062c00caa5ee5f1eac0ef44a5fb3","nasal":"f99cd13709484409037542fd504c1c4c472c6f7a24345bf16249a859dca9e3fa"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":5,"english":"Beholding the city of Kişkindhā, ruled over by Vālī, Sitā, incited by her love, addressed Rāma, with worthy words, saying","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.449,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f519857929379aebf2c99282170