:"approximate","confidence":0.461,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-125-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"218c0fa004bd3b5f38dcd3bedd0014f510eff276b61e9bc37c27cc12855197d3","compact":"dfd4f2f3ce65ddc075d610bbbab8a7dcf09fa242bdda866ae29331bdd5733880","nasal":"4a632759743f7dfa8b36f78e86abc5017e4f85da1deb77c83d139cb85a631c22"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":9,"english":"How Råma was exiled, the two boons conferred upon your mother, how king Dasaratha died in consequence of (his) sons' grief, how by emissaries, O lord, you were brought up from the house of your maternal uncle, how you did not wish for the kingdom having entered Ayodhya, how your brother, the repressor of enemies, was solicited by you for accepting the kingdom, repairing to the mount Citrakūta, who have ever wended the track of the pious, the renouncement of kingdom (by him) abiding by the words of the king, your return after taking the sandals of your revered (brother), all these, O you of long-arms, are known to you. I shall relate to you all that happened after your return.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.474,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-126-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8006c75b660118089adde81c7ccf708babe9047c664ea6bfb496d355e08991d0","compact":"835cd157d76cb8c4977aff0751caacec87d96f6b67a4f4ca1c1b7b0cbb645db6","nasal":"835cd157d76cb8c4977aff0751caacec87d96f6b67a4f4ca1c1b7b0cbb645db6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":10,"english":"There I was joined by Sugrīva, the lord of monkeys. And there I entered into an agreement, O Sita, for the destruction of Vali.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.457,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90cf94fe7cad3347cd97d42e79fa098eef786b8a60ba567c74e514c67fd0f3f7","compact":"1f20c3aa508f54806c9aec598487a0466cedb626ae0b059b9c23ee8e2ef290a6","nasal":"1f20c3aa508f54806c9aec598487a0466cedb626ae0b059b9c23ee8e2ef290a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":11,"english":"Do you behold, O Sita, Kiskindha, having beautiful gardens, the pleasant city of Sugrīva, where Vālī was slain by me.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.486,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a9f1915b482d8fe83c2fd3192032ff15690979baffe587ea3c06459cf97b32a1","compact":"860fbc3fcecbcbdb77f35ca2bff19eb4fa5cd80c623f007430beddd8099b0227","nasal":"1b50f19216b80ff74594109a3f0d7833b42a85d2c3cdb9dbe3b478d111c5897e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":12,"english":"Being thus addressed by Vaidehi Rāghava replied-saying, \"this shall be done\" and getting at Kişkindhă he stopped the car. And having beheld the car stationed he spoke to Sugriva, saying.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.464,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6154990bcd56fc2b2e81e94ec2660ec2f5cff3b4c2b3bbb72f241cc0ca8f28e2","compact":"58f01bf42b263474d3adfce49910c221d7093fdaa28ad5ef6fec4961fb19fead","nasal":"9a305c3eb7894786da1c82e462bd785dc53a2a6c6604c26065372aea92394b12"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":13,"english":"The powerful brother of the king of vultures named Sampāti communicated to us the residence of Sītā in the palace of Rāvaņa.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.432,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-126-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b2d8ddfc5a9f969f035e93184c5943f82ddd28048ef2f7cf7575d4f65ef7d843","compact":"f91774c55475e2bc25bd6cfe252cfd81aea48365cf36ed288a952f98080d85c1","nasal":"babc62fad08fe77e4ef8280c85a5b09d712c6c339a9d6b5a5113528c8d3c9df0"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":14,"english":"All those citizens, fond of piety, did not like to use good clothes beholding the prince use bark and deer skin.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.467,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-125-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f1b360e4128057cf7ed1604586b30aff6239ca9b058ec4e268e42117bca9ad8","compact":"cc7f20f89f3110c7069df7683b23e345a285e1549fbc7bfb489ce9187fa6f079","nasal":"cc7f20f89f3110c7069df7683b23e345a285e1549fbc7bfb489ce9187fa6f079"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-112-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":112,"verse":15,"english":"O king, I wish to repair to Ayodhyā your capital with you, in the company of Tārā, the dear wife of Sugrīva as well as of the wives of other leading monkeys.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.475,"method":"fuzzy-nearby-witness","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-123-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6112015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"94548777ddaa81f4bb33e2e3921ea41fc538b8335bbee6ac0c7a8567fc3e5132","compact":"3ea43cd39c6cf4b5cbf788cb9dfd032de5dad4ed6f1d6e852d1dfc92ca2cba88","nasal":"3ea43cd39c6c